### Console & Diagnostics
- Use `read_console` to read Unity Editor Console logs — **essential for diagnosing compilation errors and runtime issues**.
  - `get_errors`: Get only errors (compiler errors + runtime errors) — use this FIRST when something goes wrong.
  - `get_warnings`: Get only warnings.
  - `get_all`: Get all log entries (errors, warnings, and info logs).
  - `get_count`: Get a summary count of errors/warnings/logs without full details.
  - `clear`: Clear the console.
  - Use `search` parameter to filter entries by text (e.g., search for a specific file name or error code).
  - Use `max_entries` to control how many entries are returned (default: 50, max: 200).
- When a script modification causes compilation failure, ALWAYS call `read_console` (action: `get_errors`) to identify the exact error and file location.

